            "correct_answer": "The signal becomes the constant $1$.",
            "answer_explanation_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "Set $\\omega=0$ to get $e^{j0t}=1$. That is a constant signal, so every positive shift leaves it unchanged and the usual nonzero-period formula does not apply.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "question_index": 2,
            "question_type": "multiple-choice",
            "answer_cardinality": "single",
            "prompt_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "For $x(t)=e^{j0t}$, what is the correct repetition statement?",
